If we are using "build :" in docker-compose.yml then we need DockerFile for each project. Otherwise docker-compose.yml
will not work.

Verify the docker-compose.yml file for the school-service build context.
 It should point to the directory containing the Dockerfile:

  school-service:
    build:
      context: school  ---> it will do to school folder and try to find DockerFile to build.
      dockerfile: Dockerfile1  -->  in case you have changed Dockerfile name


2. check the sequence of build.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Remove existing containers and images:
    docker-compose down --rmi all

Clean Up Cache
  docker builder prune
  docker-compose up --build

3.You can stop all running Docker containers with the following command:
--------------------------------------------------------------------
  docker stop $(docker ps -q)

docker ps -q gives you the container IDs of all the running containers.
docker stop stops each container by ID.

4.
==================================================================================================
Clear Docker Cache
============================
docker system prune -a

